{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1550559-sorcerers-and-charms","id":1550559,"title":"Sorcerers and Charms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-05-01T17:07:55-07:00","id":1550559,"title":"Sorcerers and Charms","content":"Random question that I can't seem to find an answer to:<br /> <br /> Is there a cost to use Charms as a sorcerer? It just talks about what they are and what they can do (although not really about what you roll or what to pay).<br /> <br /> Unless I'm blind, which is possible","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1006-widdershawns","name":"widdershawns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1006_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-01T18:01:01-07:00","id":1550560,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest, reading these rules, they don't look consistent to me. Specifically, the Mindmask Condition references Sorcery rolls that don't make a lot of sense in terms of most of the charm descriptions.<br /> My suggestion off the top of my head would be to model them as a weaker, more constrained counterpart to Marvels. You get one per scene as a simple action, usually unrolled, that has no attached cost. They do what the respective section under the heading of their Working says they can do. Wonderment charms may substitute a Sorcery skill roll for whatever action the charm is duplicating, and are the primary source of appropriate charms for the Mindmask Condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","av